# Real-time Architecture & WebSocket Patterns

## WebSocket Architecture Overview

**This Poetry Slam application uses Socket.io for real-time updates with fallback mechanisms and offline support.**

### Core Real-time Features
- **Live competition updates**: Real-time participant and round status
- **Admin notifications**: Instant updates for content changes
- **Offline resilience**: Graceful degradation when WebSocket unavailable
- **Performance monitoring**: Connection health and message tracking

## WebSocket Service Architecture

### 1. Connection Management
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE connection handling
class WebSocketService {
  constructor() {
    this.socket = null;
    this.isConnected = false;
    this.isConnecting = false;
    this.subscribers = new Map();
    this.reconnectAttempts = 0;
    this.maxReconnectAttempts = 5;
    this.reconnectDelay = 2000;
    this.offlineMode = false;
    this.pendingMessages = [];
  }
  
  connect() {
    if (this.isConnecting || this.isConnected) return;
    
    this.isConnecting = true;
    this.socket = io(this.baseURL, {
      transports: ['websocket', 'polling'],
      timeout: 20000,
      forceNew: true
    });
    
    this.setupEventListeners();
  }
  
  setupEventListeners() {
    this.socket.on('connect', () => {
      this.isConnected = true;
      this.isConnecting = false;
      this.reconnectAttempts = 0;
      this.processPendingMessages();
    });
    
    this.socket.on('disconnect', () => {
      this.isConnected = false;
      this.handleDisconnection();
    });
  }
}

// ❌ OVER-ENGINEERED connection handling
class WebSocketService {
  constructor() {
    this.socket = null;
    this.connectionPool = new ConnectionPool();
    this.retryStrategy = new ExponentialBackoffStrategy();
    this.circuitBreaker = new CircuitBreaker();
    this.healthChecker = new HealthChecker();
    this.metricsCollector = new MetricsCollector();
    this.eventBus = new EventBus();
    this.stateMachine = new ConnectionStateMachine();
  }
}
```

